From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:24:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Give the PCH thermal device its minimum
 D-state

The PCH thermal controller (00:12.0) is missing from the table of the
minimum sleep states, so the PEP code prints "Unknown min d_state for
PCI: 00:12.0" twice at every boot. Add it with D3, as the other PCH
devices without a wake role.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x: the warning is gone, in the hardware test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
index 002293f67a..7139719189 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@ static struct min_sleep_state min_pci_sleep_states[] = {
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_XHCI,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_USBOTG,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_SRAM,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
+	{ PCH_DEVFN_THERMAL,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_CNViWIFI,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_SDCARD,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
 	{ PCH_DEVFN_I2C0,	ACPI_DEVICE_SLEEP_D3 },
-- 
